# Styling and Motion

## SCSS

- Entry: `src/styles/main.scss` → `@use 'variables'` + `@use 'layout'`
- Theme tokens on `:root[data-theme='light'|'dark']` — toggle via `ThemeContext` (`document.documentElement.dataset.theme`)
- Use CSS variables (`var(--text)`, `var(--accent)`) in components; avoid hardcoded colors
- Component classes: BEM-ish (`site-header`, `site-nav__link`, `content-card`)

## Theming

- Consume theme with `useTheme()` from `src/context/ThemeContext.tsrx`
- Persist preference in `localStorage` key `theme`

## Page transitions

- Route changes go through the memoized `navigate()` in `RouterContext`
- The outgoing page is a ghost clone of `.page-content` (class `page-content--exiting`) with a dark overlay; the incoming page slides in over it
- `prefers-reduced-motion` skips the clone and swaps the route immediately
- Do not add competing route animation logic in pages

## Lenis

- Shared options, the document instance, `createHorizontalLenis`, and `startLenisLoop` live in `src/lenis.ts`
- `startLenisLoop()` is called once from `src/main.ts` and drives every active instance
- The document instance ignores `.scroll-wrapper`; horizontal panels use `ScrollWrapper`
- Viewport-triggered animations subscribe to the document Lenis `scroll` event in `src/animations/`

## Entrance animations

- Import `AnimateText`, `AnimateLine`, and `AnimateContent` from `@animations`
- Omit `trigger` to play on mount; pass `viewport` (0–1) to play when the element travels through the viewport
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` — already handled inside the animation components

## GSAP elsewhere

- Import `gsap` directly; prefer transforms/opacity for performance
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` when adding new animations
